@startuml
title State diagram - Appointment lifecycle (FR-03, FR-06, FR-08, FR-16)

skinparam noteFontSize 11

state "Booked" as Booked
state "Cancelled" as Cancelled
state "Attended" as Attended
state "No-show" as NoShow

[*] --> Booked : book (FR-03) / create in free slot with UNIQUE(doctor, start)

Booked --> Cancelled : patient cancels, now <= start - 24 h (FR-06)
Booked --> Cancelled : receptionist cancels at any time (FR-06)
Booked --> Cancelled : reschedule (FR-16) / new slot booked, old one cancelled atomically
Booked --> Attended : receptionist marks attended (FR-08)
Booked --> NoShow : receptionist marks no-show (FR-08)

Cancelled --> [*] : slot is free again (US-06)
Attended --> [*] : kept for the monthly report (FR-12)
NoShow --> [*] : counted in the last 90 days (FR-09)

note right of Booked
  The only state that occupies a doctor's slot
  and counts towards the 2-future-appointments limit (FR-05).
end note

note right of NoShow
  Three no-shows in 90 days mean the patient
  may only book through reception (FR-09).
end note

@enduml
